data.content:
Created both files. Here's a summary:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Renders a `<ul>` with each item's template plus Move Up/Move Down buttons. Buttons are disabled at the list boundaries.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Code-behind with:
- **`TItem` generic** — works with any item type
- **Internal copy** — `_items` is cloned from `Items` in `SetParametersAsync`, so the parent's list is never mutated
- **`OnOrderChanged`** — fires after each swap, passing a read-only copy of the reordered list

Usage matches your example:
```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<MyTask> updated) {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
